## Summary

On cubecl backends (confirmed on metal + f16), the main `attention()` path diverges from `attention_fallback` when given a `[1, 1, seq_q, seq_kv]` broadcast bool mask. The divergence fingerprint points at the broadcast mask being applied to head 0 only, and not replicated across the remaining heads.

The equivalent test with a full-shape `[batch, heads, seq_q, seq_kv]` mask (`test_attention_all_options`) passes on the same backend, so the bug is specifically in broadcast handling.

## Minimal repro

Added to `crates/burn-backend-tests/tests/tensor/float/module/attention.rs` as part of #4777 (and currently skipped on `feature = \"cube\"` pending this issue):

\`\`\`rust
#[test]
fn test_attention_bool_mask_broadcast_batch_and_heads() {
