For now `optimizers` using the `SimpleOptimizer` trait have to return an optional state since it may not be initialized yet. We could create a new method to handle such case.

```rust
fn step<const D: usize>(
    &self,
    lr: LearningRate,
    tensor: Tensor<B, D>,
    grad: Tensor<B, D>,
    state: Self::State<D>,
) -> (Tensor<B, D>, Self::State<D>);
fn first_step<const D: usize>(
    &self,
    lr: LearningRate,
    tensor: Tensor<B, D>,
    grad: Tensor<B, D>,
) -> (Tensor<B, D>, Self::State<D>);
```

Another option is using a defined enum instead of an `Option`.

```rust
enum OptimizerState<const D: usize, O: SimpleOptimizer> {
    Uninitialized,
    State(O::State<D>),
}
```

We could also force the state to implement `Default`, but without the shape of the tensor, `Option` would probably be needed in most optimizers, not improving enough the API.

